-- title:
--   Counting Katz level-ℓ structures on an elliptic curve
-- statement:
--   Let $\Omega$ be an algebraically closed field, let $\ell$ be a prime with $3 \le \ell$ whose image in $\Omega$ is non-zero, and let $W_0$ be a Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ whose discriminant $\Delta$ is a unit. A `LevelPData` over $\Omega$ is simply a quadruple of elements $x_P, y_P, x_Q, y_Q$ of $\Omega$, and such a quadruple $D$ satisfies `IsLevelPStructure W₀ ℓ D` when: the pairs $(x_P,y_P)$ and $(x_Q,y_Q)$ both satisfy the affine Weierstrass equation of $W_0$; the division polynomial $W_0.\mathrm{pre\Psi}\,\ell$ vanishes at $x_P$ and at $x_Q$; and both of the elements $\mathrm{indepElt}\,W_0\,\ell\,x_P\,x_Q$ and $\mathrm{indepElt}\,W_0\,\ell\,x_Q\,x_P$ are units, where $$\mathrm{indepElt}\,W\,p\,x_0\,x = \prod_{a=1}^{(p-1)/2}\bigl(x\cdot (W.\Psi\mathrm{Sq}\,a)(x_0) - (W.\Phi\,a)(x_0)\bigr).$$ The theorem asserts that the number of such quadruples $D$ equals the cardinality of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/\ell)$.
--
--   The conditions say that $(x_P,y_P)$ and $(x_Q,y_Q)$ are $\ell$-torsion points of $W_0$ neither of which lies in the cyclic subgroup generated by the other, so the count is that of ordered bases of $W_0(\Omega)[\ell] \cong (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^2$, expressed entirely in division-polynomial coordinates: this is the naive form of the statement that Katz level-$\ell$ structures on an elliptic curve over an algebraically closed field are a free $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/\ell)$-orbit. It is used in the computation of the number of algebra homomorphisms realising the $j$-invariant at full level $\ell$, and in the corresponding count of Drinfeld pairs.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_natCard_levelPData_isLevelPStructure_eq_natCard_GL_of_isAlgClosed.lean

